@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1739 = private unnamed_addr constant [597 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `setattr` that take a constant attribute value as an\0Aargument (e.g., `setattr(obj, \22foo\22, 42)`).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`setattr` is used to set attributes dynamically. If the attribute is\0Adefined as a constant, it is no safer than a typical property access. When\0Apossible, prefer property access over `setattr` calls, as the former is\0Amore concise and idiomatic.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Asetattr(obj, \22foo\22, 42)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aobj.foo = 42\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `setattr`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#setattr)\0A", align 1
