@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1845 = private unnamed_addr constant [536 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `or` expressions that contain truthy values.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf the expression is used as a condition, it can be replaced in-full with\0A`True`.\0A\0AIn other cases, the expression can be short-circuited to the first truthy\0Avalue.\0A\0ABy using `True` (or the first truthy value), the code is more concise\0Aand easier to understand, since it no longer contains redundant conditions.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aif x or [1] or y:\0A    pass\0A\0Aa = x or [1] or y\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aif True:\0A    pass\0A\0Aa = x or [1]\0A```\0A", align 1
