@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1868 = private unnamed_addr constant [971 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `try`-`except`-`pass` blocks that can be replaced with the\0A`contextlib.suppress` context manager.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUsing `contextlib.suppress` is more concise and directly communicates the\0Aintent of the code: to suppress a given exception.\0A\0ANote that `contextlib.suppress` is slower than using `try`-`except`-`pass`\0Adirectly. For performance-critical code, consider retaining the\0A`try`-`except`-`pass` pattern.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    1 / 0\0Aexcept ZeroDivisionError:\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport contextlib\0A\0Awith contextlib.suppress(ZeroDivisionError):\0A    1 / 0\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `contextlib.suppress`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/contextlib.html#contextlib.suppress)\0A- [Python documentation: `try` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-try-statement)\0A- [a simpler `try`/`except` (and why maybe shouldn't)](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MZAJ8qnC7mk)\0A", align 1
