@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1898 = private unnamed_addr constant [485 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for invalid `printf`-style format strings.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AConversion specifiers are required for `printf`-style format strings. These\0Aspecifiers must contain a `%` character followed by a conversion type.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A\22Hello, %\22 % \22world\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A\22Hello, %s\22 % \22world\22\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `printf`-style String Formatting](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#printf-style-string-formatting)\0A", align 1
