@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1904 = private unnamed_addr constant [668 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for named placeholders in `printf`-style format strings without\0Amapping-type values.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen using named placeholders in `printf`-style format strings, the values\0Amust be a map type (such as a dictionary). Otherwise, the expression will\0Araise a `TypeError`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A\22%(greeting)s, %(name)s\22 % (\22Hello\22, \22World\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A\22%(greeting)s, %(name)s\22 % {\22greeting\22: \22Hello\22, \22name\22: \22World\22}\0A```\0A\0AOr:\0A```python\0A\22%s, %s\22 % (\22Hello\22, \22World\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `printf`-style String Formatting](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#printf-style-string-formatting)\0A", align 1
