@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2056 = private unnamed_addr constant [579 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for ternary `if` expressions that can be replaced with the `or`\0Aoperator.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ATernary `if` expressions are more verbose than `or` expressions while\0Aproviding the same functionality.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Az = x if x else y\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Az = x or y\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe in the event that the body of the\0A`if` expression contains side effects.\0A\0AFor example, `foo` will be called twice in `foo() if foo() else bar()`\0A(assuming `foo()` returns a truthy value), but only once in\0A`foo() or bar()`.\0A", align 1
@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2057 = private unnamed_addr constant [50 x i8] c"Replace ternary `if` expression with `or` operator", align 1
