@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2091 = private unnamed_addr constant [34 x i8] c"ruff-static-key-dict-comprehension", align 1
@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2092 = private unnamed_addr constant [722 x i8] c"## Removed\0AThis rule was implemented in `flake8-bugbear` and has been remapped to [B035]\0A\0A## What it does\0AChecks for dictionary comprehensions that use a static key, like a string\0Aliteral or a variable defined outside the comprehension.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUsing a static key (like a string literal) in a dictionary comprehension\0Ais usually a mistake, as it will result in a dictionary with only one key,\0Adespite the comprehension iterating over multiple values.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adata = [\22some\22, \22Data\22]\0A{\22key\22: value.upper() for value in data}\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adata = [\22some\22, \22Data\22]\0A{value: value.upper() for value in data}\0A```\0A\0A[B035]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/static-key-dict-comprehension/\0A", align 1
